# e17_status.gbnf: the three literals of rules_e17.c, letter for letter, and the three
# sentence field report beside them. The key is named "state" and not the house name
# "decision" on purpose, because the state of a modem is what the chapter calls it;
# the cost is that tools/agreement.py, which reads a "decision" key, does not apply to
# this project and projects/e17-cellular-summariser/tools/hallucination_check.py reads
# the "state" key instead and prints the agreement table itself. The report is 40 to
# 400 characters from letters, digits, space, comma, full stop, percent, plus and
# minus, so it can carry neither a quote nor a brace nor a newline, and it ends with a
# full stop, so the end of generation token is reachable only after a complete
# sentence. The stub expands the first alternative on every path and a character class
# to nothing, so in CI the answer is {"state":"OK","report":"."}, which
# tests/oracle/e17.expected.csv expects on every model answered row. ws admits spaces
# and tabs, never a newline.
root   ::= "{" ws "\"state\"" ws ":" ws state ws "," ws "\"report\"" ws ":" ws report ws "}"
state  ::= "\"OK\"" | "\"DEGRADED\"" | "\"DOWN\""
report ::= "\"" [A-Za-z0-9 ,.%+-]{39,399} "." "\""
ws     ::= [ \t]*
